From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HuanPo Lin <robertlin@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 06:46:29 -0700
Subject: Fix BrowserInterfaceBrokerImpl and MojoBinderPolicyApplier lifetime
 with kLazyBrowserInterfaceBroker

When `features::kLazyBrowserInterfaceBroker` is enabled,
`RenderFrameHostImpl::broker_holder_` is created lazily and may be
destroyed before prerender activation (e.g., when
`TearDownMojoConnection()` is called on a subframe). Previously, this
caused two issues during prerendering: 1.
`BrowserInterfaceBrokerImpl::GetInterface()` passed
   `base::Unretained(this)` callbacks to `MojoBinderPolicyApplier`
   under the assumption that the broker always outlived the policy
   applier. Destroying `broker_holder_` before activation left dangling
   deferred callbacks in `MojoBinderPolicyApplier` (causing a UAF upon
   activation) and triggered `CHECK(broker_holder_)` in
   `RendererDidActivateForPrerendering()`.
2. `mojo_binder_policy_applier_` was created inside
   `CreateBrokerHolder()`, and `broker_holder_` was reset whenever the
   `BrowserInterfaceBroker` receiver was rebound, unintentionally
   resetting `MojoBinderPolicyApplier` state (such as
   `Mode::kPrepareToGrantAll`).

This CL fixes these issues by:
- Calling `policy_applier_->DropDeferredBinders()` in
  `~BrowserInterfaceBrokerImpl()` so pending callbacks targeting the
  broker are dropped upon destruction.
- Clearing `deferred_sync_binders_` in
  `MojoBinderPolicyApplier::DropDeferredBinders()`.
- Initializing `mojo_binder_policy_applier_` in the
  `RenderFrameHostImpl` constructor when prerendering, and preserving
  `broker_holder_` across `BrowserInterfaceBroker` receiver rebinds.
- Guarding `broker_holder_` accesses in
  `RendererDidActivateForPrerendering()` and `DidCommitNavigation()`.

